 60ZN    60GA EC+B+ DECAY (69.4 MS)    2001MA96,2021OR01,2025OW01ENSDF    202509
 60ZN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$                                    
 60ZN2 H CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$                                             
 60ZN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=E. BROWNE, J. K. TULI$                                     
 60ZN2 H CIT=NDS 114, 1849 (2013)$CUT=31-Dec-2012$                              
 60ZN dE EAV,LOGFT$FROM BetaShape v2.4 (Jun-2024) 2023Mo21.                     
 60ZN dG CC$FROM BrIcc v2.3e (17-Jun-2020) 2008Ki07, "Frozen Orbitals" appr.    
 60ZN dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 11-Nov-2025)          
 60ZN c  2001Ma96: {+60}Ga was produced via the {+28}Si({+36}Ar,p3n) fusion     
 60ZN2c  evaporation reaction using a 4.71 MeV/u {+36}Ar primary beam at the GSI
 60ZN3c  On-Line Mass Separator. A 55-keV {+60}Ga{+1+} beam was extracted and   
 60ZN4c  implanted into a tape for |b|g measurements and carbon foils for |bp   
 60ZN5c  and |b|a measurements in a beam-on/beam-off mode. Positrons were       
 60ZN6c  detected using a plastic scintillator and |g rays were detected using  
 60ZN7c  Ge detectors. Particles were detected using Si |DE-E telescopes at     
 60ZN8c  another beam line. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |b|g-coin, E{-p}(>0.6 
 60ZN9c  MeV), I{-p}, E{-|a}, and I{-|a}. Deduced levels, J, |p, {+60}Ga        
 60ZNAc  T{-1/2}, and {+60}Ga mass using the known {+60}Zn mass, the E|g from   
 60ZNBc  the T=1 IAS in {+60}Zn, and the Coulomb displacement energy systematics
 60ZNCc  (1997An07). Identified a total of 802 proton events and deduced        
 60ZNDc  %(|e+|b{++})p=1.6 {I7}. Identified 9 |a candidate events and deduced   
 60ZNEc  %(|e+|b{++})|a<0.023 {I20}.                                            
 60ZN c  2021Or01: {+60}Ga was produced via the projectile fragmentation of a   
 60ZN2c  345-MeV/u {+78}Kr primary beam impinging on a 5-mm thick {+9}Be target,
 60ZN3c  identified in the RIKEN BigRIPS separator by B|r-|DE-ToF, transported  
 60ZN4c  to the exit of the ZeroDegree spectrometer, and implanted into the     
 60ZN5c  Wide-range Active Silicon Strip Stopper Array for Beta and ion         
 60ZN6c  detection (WAS3ABi) consisting of three 1-mm-thick DSSDs. |g rays were 
 60ZN7c  detected using the EUroball-RIKEN Cluster Array of 12 cluster-type Ge  
 60ZN8c  detectors. Measured E{-p}(>1.5 MeV), E|g, I|g, p|g-coin, |b|g-coin,    
 60ZN9c  |g|g-coin, and implant-decay time correlations. Deduced levels, {+60}Ga
 60ZNAc  T{-1/2}, and {+60}Ga mass using the known {+59}Zn mass, the E{-p} and  
 60ZNBc  E|g from the T=2 IAS in {+60}Ga populated by {+60}Ge decay in the same 
 60ZNCc  experiment.                                                            
 60ZN c  2025Ow01: {+60}Ga was produced via the projectile fragmentation of a   
 60ZN2c  150-MeV/nucleon {+78}Kr{+36+} primary beam impinging on a 517-mg/cm{+2}
 60ZN3c  thick {+9}Be target, filtered by the NSCL A1900 separator and the radio
 60ZN4c  frequency fragment separator, identified using the |DE-ToF method, and 
 60ZN5c  implanted into a 1-mm-thick DSSD with 16|*16 1.2-mm wide strips at the 
 60ZN6c  center of the Summing NaI (SuN) detector. Beam ions and decay positrons
 60ZN7c  were detected using the DSSD and |g rays were detected using the SuN   
 60ZN8c  detector. Measured implant-decay correlations, |g-ray total absorption 
 60ZN9c  spectra (TAS), sum of segments spectra (SoS), and multiplicity spectra.
 60ZNAc  Deduced |b-feeding intensities, Gamow-Teller strength distributions,   
 60ZNBc  and T{-1/2} of parent {+60}Ga. Compared with shell-model calculations  
 60ZNCc  using GXPF1A and KB3G Hamiltonians.                                    
 60ZN cE IB,IE,LOGFT$Calculated by evaluators using the BetaShape code          
 60ZN2cE (2023Mo21).                                                            
 60ZN cE TI$From 2025Ow01. I(|e+|b{++}) at each E(level) is extracted by        
 60ZN2cE simultaneously fitting the simulated TAS, SoS, and multiplicity spectra
 60ZN3cE to data via the |h{+2} minimization. The sum is normalized to          
 60ZN4cE |S%I(|e+|b{++})=100. The decay scheme built via |b-delayed |g-ray      
 60ZN5cE spectroscopy (2001Ma96,2021Or01) is considered incomplete due to a     
 60ZN6cE large gap of 9 MeV between the highest observed level at E=4852 and    
 60ZN7cE Q(|e)=14160 {I15}. There should be missing transitions from unobserved 
 60ZN8cE levels in the gap. Therefore, the |e+|b{++}-feeding values from |g+ce  
 60ZN9cE intensity balance at each level are considered upper limits due to the 
 60ZNAcE incomplete decay scheme.                                               
 60ZN cE TI(A)$I(|e+|b{++}) values below 0.1 were set to 0.0 in 2025Ow01 due to 
 60ZN2cE sensitivity limitations.                                               
 60ZN cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies for levels connected with
 60ZN2cL |g transitions. For other levels below 5.3 MeV, from 2025Ow01 adopted  
 60ZN3cL from the RIPL-3 library, originally from the Adopted Levels of {+60}Zn 
 60ZN4cL (2013Br15) rounded to the nearest keV. For levels above 5.3 MeV,       
 60ZN5cL E(level) is a sample of calculated continuum-state energies with energy
 60ZN6cL spacing (273 keV) that follows the energy resolution of the SuN        
 60ZN7cL detector.                                                              
 60GA  P 0            2+               69.4 MS   2              14160     15    
